NAME
  disco - Find computers and services on the network

SYNOPIS
  disco start [name] [--services=svc=value,...] [--ttl=seconds]
  disco stop
  disco offer <service> [value]
  disco withdraw <service>
  disco status
  disco find [service] [--timeout=seconds]
  disco resolve <name> [--timeout=seconds]
  disco list

DESCRIPTION
  Computers that run "disco start" answer queries for their name and the services they offer.
  Name defaults to /etc/hostname. Answers are cached until their ttl (default 120s) runs out.
  disco only tells you who is reachable right now; use pair to trust a host and share secrets.
  Uses port 5353 on every modem. To announce at boot, enable the disco rc service.

EXAMPLES
  disco start hub --services=craftServer=5990
    Announce this computer as "hub" offering craftServer on port 5990

  disco find craftServer
    List every computer offering craftServer

  disco resolve hub
    Print the modem address of "hub"
